    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="1245" n="1231" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1380: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-30">March 30,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received March 30—1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1935. Sequence Legation’s 631 January 31.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d772-f1"/> Berlin
                    despatches 29th state Wilhelmstrasse spokesman in reply to inspired question
                    declared “preparations for trial of captured Allied soldiers charged with war
                    crimes are now well advanced”. Despatches add spokesman referred to American and
                    British as well as Russian prisoners but intimated such trials would not
                    actually take place unless new trials took place against German prisoners in
                    hands United Nations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d772-f1" n="12" xml:id="d772-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it cited a German news report that “Proceedings against English and
                    American war prisoners envisaged in connection with Charkov trials are in
                    preparation state.” (740.00116 European War/1289)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
